# Prisma and MySQL

Provider is `mysql`. Prisma is 7.10.1. The schema is a folder. The generator is `prisma-client` with `moduleFormat = "cjs"` and output `src/generated/prisma`. Do not put `prismaSchemaFolder` or `relationJoins` in `previewFeatures`. The CLI database URL lives in `prisma.config.ts`. Auth models stay in `prisma/schema/auth.prisma`. Content models stay beside `Article`.

```prisma
exampleId String @id @default(uuid(7)) @db.Char(40)
```

Services omit that id. Prisma Client fills a UUID version 7. Do not use `autoincrement()` for these keys, and do not add a MySQL `UUID()` default. `UserRefreshToken.userRefreshTokenId` has no default; `AuthService` sets it with `randomBytes`. Seeded role and user ids stay `SUPERADMIN` and `ADMIN`.

- Generate with `yarn prisma migrate dev --name <name> --create-only`, then read the SQL.
- On a populated table, add a required column as nullable, backfill every row, then set `NOT NULL` in that same file.
- Keep one migration per change. Do not reset or squash unless the user asks.
- Seed permissions with role id `SUPERADMIN` or `ADMIN`. Role names are `SUPER ADMIN` and `ADMIN`.
- Do not print `DATABASE_URL` or `env.conf` secrets.
